{{also|Tauchen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|tūchen|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term||-tūhhan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*dūkaną}}. Cognate to {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|duiken|lang=de}}. The word had become widely obsolete in Upper German, but was later revived on the basis of {{etyl|gml|de}} {{term|dūken|lang=gml}} and Central German {{term||dūchen|lang=gmh}}, which had remained common. In the course of this process, the originally strong verb became weak. A derivative with Low German consonantism is {{term|ducken|lang=de}} (cognate to and synonymous with the English verb {{term|duck|lang=en}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtaʊ̯xən/|[ˈtaʊ̯xən]|[ˈtaʊ̯xn̩]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-tauchen.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|tau|chen|lang=de}}

